03:42:35.490 --> 03:42:37.670
14 of the New Zealand Bill of Rights Act.

3649
03:42:38.730 --> 03:42:42.650
Begging is a form of expression. This was noted by the Attorney General in

3650
03:42:42.670 --> 03:42:46.370
his report, who stated that a person who is begging is conveying the

3651
03:42:46.430 --> 03:42:48.850
message, "I'm in need, and I'm requesting your help."

3652
03:42:51.930 --> 03:42:53.770
The right to freedom of expression

3653
03:42:55.470 --> 03:42:59.100
is protected for good reason. Freedom of expression is

3654
03:42:59.130 --> 03:43:01.950
fundamentally important to any democratic society.

3655
03:43:02.490 --> 03:43:05.430
Without it, we cannot claim to be free at all.

3656
03:43:06.770 --> 03:43:10.230
Much of the justification that has been provided for the bill has

3657
03:43:10.250 --> 03:43:13.110
concerned threatening and disorderly behavior.

3658
03:43:13.650 --> 03:43:17.530
So for example, in an interview, the Prime Minister gave the example of tourists

3659
03:43:17.590 --> 03:43:21.380
being confronted by a person sitting at a storefront, threatening at

3660
03:43:21.430 --> 03:43:23.130
them, shouting at them, and abusing them.

3661
03:43:24.690 --> 03:43:28.580
However, the definition of begging in clause four of the bill is quite broad and

3662
03:43:28.590 --> 03:43:31.510
is not restricted to begging that is disorderly or aggressive in

3663
03:43:31.570 --> 03:43:35.540
nature. A person could be issued a move on order therefore

3664
03:43:35.570 --> 03:43:39.470
for peacefully or even silently begging.

3665
03:43:39.510 --> 03:43:42.810
Because a person who fails to comply with the move on order commits a criminal

3666
03:43:42.870 --> 03:43:46.730
offense, the bill would in effect criminalize a peaceful form of

3667
03:43:46.790 --> 03:43:47.430
expression.

3668
03:43:49.090 --> 03:43:52.950
Another justification that has been used by the government for the ban on

3669
03:43:53.010 --> 03:43:56.810
begging is that it is necessary to support thriving urban economies.

3670
03:43:57.570 --> 03:44:01.230
We would like to ask though, how does a person peacefully begging actually

3671
03:44:01.310 --> 03:44:03.370
prevent an urban economy from thriving?

3672
03:44:04.010 --> 03:44:07.410
Because such a person, as we noted in our submission, is not disrupting passersby

3673
03:44:07.850 --> 03:44:09.370
or preventing them from entering shops.

3674
03:44:10.790 --> 03:44:14.770
In our view, it seems quite likely that the ban on begging serves to alleviate

3675
03:44:14.780 --> 03:44:18.310
the discomfort that some may feel when they see a person begging on the street.

3676
03:44:19.350 --> 03:44:23.219
However, that is not a sound reason to curtail a fundamental democratic

3677
03:44:23.310 --> 03:44:23.690
right.

3678
03:44:24.529 --> 03:44:27.630
There are many forms of expression that may offend certain people's

3679
03:44:27.670 --> 03:44:31.270
sensibilities. The beauty of living in a free and democratic

3680
03:44:31.280 --> 03:44:34.890
society is that these forms of expression are nevertheless

3681
03:44:34.910 --> 03:44:35.460
protected.

3682
03:44:36.900 --> 03:44:40.520
The rights to freedom of expression should only be curtailed for

3683
03:44:40.550 --> 03:44:44.310
exceptionally good reasons. That is recognized by Section

3684
03:44:44.590 --> 03:44:48.250
5 of BORA. The government has not provided any good

3685
03:44:48.290 --> 03:44:50.170
reasons. Over to you, Fergus.

3686
03:44:52.790 --> 03:44:56.360
Freedom of movement is a right guaranteed to all New Zealanders under the New

3687
03:44:56.410 --> 03:44:57.430
Zealand Bill of Rights Act.

3688
03:44:58.510 --> 03:45:01.980
It protects people's ability to pursue their own personal endeavors without

3689
03:45:02.030 --> 03:45:03.070
interference from the government.

3690
03:45:04.440 --> 03:45:08.270
Amnesty Youth Otago is concerned about individuals' freedom of movement being

3691
03:45:08.310 --> 03:45:12.270
interfered with by the bill. The bill gives wide-ranging powers to

3692
03:45:12.290 --> 03:45:16.210
police to move on individuals with limited restrictions.

3693
03:45:16.270 --> 03:45:19.360
There is no specification as to what a specified distance is,

3694
03:45:20.290 --> 03:45:23.970
nor are there carve-outs for entering an area which one has been moved on from

3695
03:45:24.530 --> 03:45:28.250
for important purposes such as going to a doctor or accessing

3696
03:45:28.330 --> 03:45:29.590
other essential services.

3697
03:45:31.130 --> 03:45:34.940
More guidance or restriction should be included as to what specified

3698
03:45:35.010 --> 03:45:38.330
distance means, and carve-outs for access to essential services

3699
03:45:38.790 --> 03:45:39.910
need to be included.

3700
03:45:41.160 --> 03:45:44.970
We do not consider the provision in Section 8F of the bill

3701
03:45:45.490 --> 03:45:49.010
that allows someone to breach a move on order if they have reasonable excuse to be

3702
03:45:49.330 --> 03:45:53.150
a sufficient enough carve-out, as it provides very little detail as

3703
03:45:53.230 --> 03:45:55.590
when one does have a reasonable excuse.

3704
03:45:56.150 --> 03:45:57.370
The law needs to be clear.

3705
03:45:58.570 --> 03:46:02.090
We also have concerns that rough sleeping being included as a ground for moving

3706
03:46:02.590 --> 03:46:03.010
someone on.

3707
03:46:04.530 --> 03:46:08.430
Rough sleeping in and of itself does not interfere with others' uses

3708
03:46:08.470 --> 03:46:09.320
of public spaces.

3709
03:46:10.310 --> 03:46:14.250
Public spaces are meant to be there for everyone, including those who may

3710
03:46:14.290 --> 03:46:18.030
be rough sleeping. Providing police with power to move on rough

3711
03:46:18.070 --> 03:46:21.850
sleepers prevents them from using public spaces that are meant to be for them.

3712
03:46:24.230 --> 03:46:27.610
Moving on rough sleepers will also likely see them moving further out of the CBD,

3713
03:46:28.230 --> 03:46:31.650
as there's insufficient night shelter capacity, as highlighted in the case of

3714
03:46:31.670 --> 03:46:35.230
Auckland, towards less well-lit, less trafficked,

3715
03:46:35.630 --> 03:46:37.610
and ultimately less safe areas.

3716
03:46:38.490 --> 03:46:41.030
I'll pass to Nico to discuss the further impact on the homeless.

3717
03:46:42.570 --> 03:46:46.270
Thank you, Fergus. So I lastly just briefly want to address the significant harm

3718
03:46:46.310 --> 03:46:48.350
that we believe this bill will cause to the homeless community.

3719
03:46:49.390 --> 03:46:53.090
Firstly, the move on orders process itself will obviously likely result in stress,

3720
03:46:53.550 --> 03:46:55.650
and could make the lives of homeless people more dangerous.

3721
03:46:56.730 --> 03:46:58.770
As I'm sure you've heard from previous submitters,

3722
03:46:59.590 --> 03:47:03.230
people occupy the center of towns and cities because they are the safest

3723
03:47:03.240 --> 03:47:07.050
places to be. They have lighting, there are other people in the homeless community

3724
03:47:07.090 --> 03:47:08.950
nearby, and there are central services nearby.

3725
03:47:10.770 --> 03:47:13.290
So I don't think it's necessary to elaborate too much on that, but that is

3726
03:47:14.250 --> 03:47:18.050
quite a key concern of ours. And I would also like to point out that it does not

3727
03:47:18.070 --> 03:47:21.210
appear that sufficient thought has gone into the true impact that the bill will

3728
03:47:21.270 --> 03:47:23.250
have on the homeless community.

3729
03:47:24.170 --> 03:47:28.060
Two weeks ago, well after this bill had been introduced to the House, the Prime

3730
03:47:28.130 --> 03:47:31.250
Minister admitted he didn't know there was no night shelter for rough sleepers in

3731
03:47:31.310 --> 03:47:31.750
Auckland.

3732
03:47:32.690 --> 03:47:35.950
The truth is that many people living on the street simply have nowhere else to

3733
03:47:35.970 --> 03:47:39.650
go. If they are moved on by the police, the question is

3734
03:47:39.730 --> 03:47:41.930
what exactly ought they to do?

3735
03:47:43.230 --> 03:47:46.010
We think the bill just doesn't address this core question

3736
03:47:46.550 --> 03:47:50.470
sufficiently. So in closing, AOL recommends that the bill

3737
03:47:50.510 --> 03:47:53.770
not proceed on the basis that it unjustifiably restricts the rights of New

3738
03:47:53.830 --> 03:47:57.589
Zealanders, is unnecessary, and will result in harm being caused to the

3739
03:47:57.610 --> 03:48:00.870
homeless community, and at the very least, that rough sleeping and begging should

3740
03:48:00.910 --> 03:48:03.730
be removed as grounds for issuing a move on order. Happy to take questions.

3741
03:48:04.690 --> 03:48:07.750
